                        "glosses": [
                            "Ted Kaczynski, the perpetrator of mail bomb attacks in America between 1978 and 1994, so named by the media."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fc1307ad-8e90-4a82-9f1a-888868046ba5",
                                "sense_id": "1610cbb5-7556-35af-a2c1-7cc662bb5f3e",
                                "text": "Based on the Unabomber’s manifesto, the smash movie of twenty thirty-four will be Barbarians in the Gates, the autobiographical return-to-nature philosophy of Bill Gates, Jr. Starring Oscar-winner, actor Cody Gifford."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d7f4d226-12b9-498c-9150-a22f4debe5e3",
                                "sense_id": "1610cbb5-7556-35af-a2c1-7cc662bb5f3e",
                                "text": "As a piece of writing, the rambling and often contradictory manifesto has the pathos of the Unabomber manifesto but lacks the ideological coherency."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c32418c3-b9ca-4c79-9594-bcd28410f34f",
                                "sense_id": "1610cbb5-7556-35af-a2c1-7cc662bb5f3e",
                                "text": "First, the president’s uncle died in 1985. Kaczynski was publicly revealed as the Unabomber more than a decade later, in 1996, when he was captured; before that, he had lived as a recluse in the Montana wilderness."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
